# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/

# Node
node_modules/
dist/
.vite/

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Output — plots and paperwork are generated, not committed
out/
*.pdf
*.dxf
!samples/*.dxf

# Editor
.vscode/
.idea/

# node
web/node_modules/

# Plots a designer saves from the editor. User data, not repo content.
plots/

# The built editor. NOT committed — it is a build artifact, and a stale one in
# git is worse than none. The release workflow builds it into the download.
web/dist/

# Written into the package by the release workflow, from the tag. A checkout
# must never have one — a working copy that claims a released version sends
# somebody hunting a bug in source that is not what they are running.
server/plotedit/VERSION

# Written at release time from the tag annotation, then checked and published.
release-notes.md

# Claude Code's own folder. It holds launch.json — which dev server to start for
# the in-app browser — and is a local tool's config, not part of the project.
# ⚠ This repository is PUBLIC, so anything that lands here lands in front of
# everybody; ignoring it is the cheap way to make sure nothing does by accident.
.claude/

# A show model exported out of a real production, and the images it carries.
# ⚠ THE IMAGE RULE COVERS THE FAMILY, NOT ONE EXTENSION. A venue photograph
# is as likely to be a .png as a .jpg, and a half-closed hole reads as a
# closed one. Nothing in this repo tracks an image, so none is at risk.
#
# 🔴 AND BOTH CASES, BECAUSE GITIGNORE IS CASE-SENSITIVE WHERE IT COUNTS.
# macOS sets core.ignoreCase=true, so *.png catches plan.PNG there and the
# gap is invisible on the machine these are written on. CI runs Linux, where
# it does not — and a camera still writes IMG_1234.JPG.
# ⚠ SAME REASON AS .claude/ ABOVE, and a sharper one. These land here by hand
# while somebody is testing the importer against a real job, and an exported
# model's <title> is the SHOW AND THE VENUE — a client's name, one `git add -A`
# from a public repo. Three copies of one had been sitting untracked since
# 15 Oct, none of them ignored.
#
# ⚠ `_m.html` is deliberately narrow: web/index.html is the editor itself and
# is tracked, so nothing wider than the exact name can be used here.
_m.html
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.png
*.JPG
*.JPEG
*.PNG
web/public/
